# Facts for the reload tier routing decision (reload_ladder.py _run_ladder / _handle_guard_wedge).
# guard_wedged is the result of _t2_5_guard_check (bool or None; None counts as not-wedged).
# main_dead is set when the main Unity process cannot respond (diagnose fell back to reload channel).
# runner_active is True when an osascript_runner is supplied (macOS Accessibility path, T4).
# consent_given maps to play_stop_consent: caller authorised Play/Stop cycle (T5).
# Outputs: guardBlocked → GUARD-WEDGED stop; t5Guard → skip T3/T4 jump to T5; t3Ahead → run T3;
#          t4Ahead → run T4 (main dead, runner present); t5Ahead → run T5; manualRequired → no path.
CONTRACT unitymcp.reloadtier
COVERAGE declared-scope
MODULE reloadtier_facts
FACT tier.guardWedged bool
FACT tier.mainDead bool
FACT tier.runnerActive bool
FACT tier.consentGiven bool
INPUT reloadRoute tier.guardWedged tier.mainDead tier.runnerActive tier.consentGiven
